What is Healthcare Supply Chain Management?
Healthcare Supply Chain Management (HCSCM) refers to the systematic coordination of manufacturing, sourcing, inventory, distribution, and logistics activities that deliver medical products, devices, and pharmaceuticals to healthcare providers. By integrating data from suppliers, manufacturers, hospitals, and pharmacies, HCSCM enables real time visibility, reduces stock outs, optimizes inventory levels, and supports compliance with regulatory requirements such as the Drug Supply Chain Security Act.
